            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-27534",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-27534"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2023-27534?s=ubuntu&n=curl&ns=ubuntu&t=deb&osn=ubuntu&osv=22.04&vr=%3C7.81.0-1ubuntu1.10",
              "help": {
                "text": "A path traversal vulnerability exists in curl <8.0.0 SFTP implementation causes the tilde (~) character to be wrongly replaced when used as a prefix in the first path element, in addition to its intended use as the first element to indicate a path relative to the user's home directory. Attackers can exploit this flaw to bypass filtering or execute arbitrary code by crafting a path like /~2/foo while accessing a server with a specific user.\n",
                "markdown": "> A path traversal vulnerability exists in curl <8.0.0 SFTP implementation causes the tilde (~) character to be wrongly replaced when used as a prefix in the first path element, in addition to its intended use as the first element to indicate a path relative to the user's home directory. Attackers can exploit this flaw to bypass filtering or execute arbitrary code by crafting a path like /~2/foo while accessing a server with a specific user.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                                      |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:deb/ubuntu/curl@7.81.0-1ubuntu1.3?os_distro=jammy&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=22.04  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <7.81.0-1ubuntu1.10                                                                    |\n|Fixed version                                                                  7.81.0-1ubuntu1.10                                                                     |\n|[[CVSS Score 8.8] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H]]                                                                                         |\n"
