            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-28321",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-28321"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2022-28321?s=ubuntu&n=pam&ns=ubuntu&t=deb&osn=ubuntu&osv=22.04&vr=%3C1.4.0-11ubuntu2.1",
              "help": {
                "text": "The Linux-PAM package before 1.5.2-6.1 for openSUSE Tumbleweed allows authentication bypass for SSH logins. The pam_access.so module doesn't correctly restrict login if a user tries to connect from an IP address that is not resolvable via DNS. In such conditions, a user with denied access to a machine can still get access. NOTE: the relevance of this issue is largely limited to openSUSE Tumbleweed and openSUSE Factory; it does not affect Linux-PAM upstream.\n",
                "markdown": "> The Linux-PAM package before 1.5.2-6.1 for openSUSE Tumbleweed allows authentication bypass for SSH logins. The pam_access.so module doesn't correctly restrict login if a user tries to connect from an IP address that is not resolvable via DNS. In such conditions, a user with denied access to a machine can still get access. NOTE: the relevance of this issue is largely limited to openSUSE Tumbleweed and openSUSE Factory; it does not affect Linux-PAM upstream.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                                   |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:deb/ubuntu/pam@1.4.0-11ubuntu2?os_distro=jammy&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=22.04  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <1.4.0-11ubuntu2.1                                                                  |\n|Fixed version                                                                  1.4.0-11ubuntu2.1                                                                   |\n|[[CVSS Score 9.8] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H]]                                                                                      |\n"
