            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-12243",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-12243"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2024-12243?s=ubuntu&n=gnutls28&ns=ubuntu&t=deb&osn=ubuntu&osv=22.04&vr=%3C3.7.3-4ubuntu1.6",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GnuTLS, which relies on libtasn1 for ASN.1 data processing. Due to an inefficient algorithm in libtasn1, decoding certain DER-encoded certificate data can take excessive time, leading to increased resource consumption. This flaw allows a remote attacker to send a specially crafted certificate, causing GnuTLS to become unresponsive or slow, resulting in a denial-of-service condition.\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in GnuTLS, which relies on libtasn1 for ASN.1 data processing. Due to an inefficient algorithm in libtasn1, decoding certain DER-encoded certificate data can take excessive time, leading to increased resource consumption. This flaw allows a remote attacker to send a specially crafted certificate, causing GnuTLS to become unresponsive or slow, resulting in a denial-of-service condition.\n\n|                                                                                                        |\n|Package         pkg:deb/ubuntu/gnutls28@3.7.3-4ubuntu1?os_distro=jammy&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=22.04  |\n|Affected range  <3.7.3-4ubuntu1.6                                                                       |\n|Fixed version   3.7.3-4ubuntu1.6                                                                        |\n"
              },
