              "help": {
                "text": "less through 653 allows OS command execution via a newline character in the name of a file, because quoting is mishandled in filename.c. Exploitation typically requires use with attacker-controlled file names, such as the files extracted from an untrusted archive. Exploitation also requires the LESSOPEN environment variable, but this is set by default in many common cases.\n",
                "markdown": "> less through 653 allows OS command execution via a newline character in the name of a file, because quoting is mishandled in filename.c. Exploitation typically requires use with attacker-controlled file names, such as the files extracted from an untrusted archive. Exploitation also requires the LESSOPEN environment variable, but this is set by default in many common cases.\n\n|                                                                                                 |\n|Package         pkg:deb/ubuntu/less@590-1build1?os_distro=jammy&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=22.04  |\n|Affected range  <590-1ubuntu0.22.04.3                                                            |\n|Fixed version   590-1ubuntu0.22.04.3                                                             |\n"
