            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-8096",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-8096"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2024-8096?s=ubuntu&n=curl&ns=ubuntu&t=deb&osn=ubuntu&osv=22.04&vr=%3C7.81.0-1ubuntu1.18",
              "help": {
                "text": "When curl is told to use the Certificate Status Request TLS extension, often referred to as OCSP stapling, to verify that the server certificate is valid, it might fail to detect some OCSP problems and instead wrongly consider the response as fine.  If the returned status reports another error than 'revoked' (like for example 'unauthorized') it is not treated as a bad certficate.\n",
                "markdown": "> When curl is told to use the Certificate Status Request TLS extension, often referred to as OCSP stapling, to verify that the server certificate is valid, it might fail to detect some OCSP problems and instead wrongly consider the response as fine.  If the returned status reports another error than 'revoked' (like for example 'unauthorized') it is not treated as a bad certficate.\n\n|                                                                                                       |\n|Package         pkg:deb/ubuntu/curl@7.81.0-1ubuntu1.3?os_distro=jammy&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=22.04  |\n|Affected range  <7.81.0-1ubuntu1.18                                                                    |\n|Fixed version   7.81.0-1ubuntu1.18                                                                     |\n"
