            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-4877",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-4877"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-4877?s=ubuntu&n=libssh&ns=ubuntu&t=deb&osn=ubuntu&osv=22.04&vr=%3C0.9.6-2ubuntu0.22.04.4",
              "help": {
                "text": "There's a vulnerability in the libssh package where when a libssh consumer passes in an unexpectedly large input buffer to ssh_get_fingerprint_hash() function. In such cases the bin_to_base64() function can experience an integer overflow leading to a memory under allocation, when that happens it's possible that the program perform out of bounds write leading to a heap corruption. This issue affects only 32-bits builds of libssh.\n",
                "markdown": "> There's a vulnerability in the libssh package where when a libssh consumer passes in an unexpectedly large input buffer to ssh_get_fingerprint_hash() function. In such cases the bin_to_base64() function can experience an integer overflow leading to a memory under allocation, when that happens it's possible that the program perform out of bounds write leading to a heap corruption. This issue affects only 32-bits builds of libssh.\n\n|                                                                                                     |\n|Package         pkg:deb/ubuntu/libssh@0.9.6-2build1?os_distro=jammy&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=22.04  |\n|Affected range  <0.9.6-2ubuntu0.22.04.4                                                              |\n|Fixed version   0.9.6-2ubuntu0.22.04.4                                                               |\n"
              },
