            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-4878",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-4878"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-4878?s=ubuntu&n=libssh&ns=ubuntu&t=deb&osn=ubuntu&osv=22.04&vr=%3C0.9.6-2ubuntu0.22.04.4",
              "help": {
                "text": "A vulnerability was found in libssh, where an uninitialized variable exists under certain conditions in the privatekey_from_file() function. This flaw can be triggered if the file specified by the filename doesn't exist and may lead to possible signing failures or heap corruption.\n",
