            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-5372",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-5372"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-5372?s=ubuntu&n=libssh&ns=ubuntu&t=deb&osn=ubuntu&osv=22.04&vr=%3C0.9.6-2ubuntu0.22.04.4",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in libssh versions built with OpenSSL versions older than 3.0, specifically in the ssh_kdf() function responsible for key derivation. Due to inconsistent interpretation of return values where OpenSSL uses 0 to indicate failure and libssh uses 0 for success—the function may mistakenly return a success status even when key derivation fails. This results in uninitialized cryptographic key buffers being used in subsequent communication, potentially compromising SSH sessions' confidentiality, integrity, and availability.\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in libssh versions built with OpenSSL versions older than 3.0, specifically in the ssh_kdf() function responsible for key derivation. Due to inconsistent interpretation of return values where OpenSSL uses 0 to indicate failure and libssh uses 0 for success—the function may mistakenly return a success status even when key derivation fails. This results in uninitialized cryptographic key buffers being used in subsequent communication, potentially compromising SSH sessions' confidentiality, integrity, and availability.\n\n|                                                                                                     |\n|Package         pkg:deb/ubuntu/libssh@0.9.6-2build1?os_distro=jammy&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=22.04  |\n|Affected range  <0.9.6-2ubuntu0.22.04.4                                                              |\n|Fixed version   0.9.6-2ubuntu0.22.04.4                                                               |\n"
              },
