            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-58183",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-58183"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-58183?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.24.8",
              "help": {
                "text": "tar.Reader does not set a maximum size on the number of sparse region data blocks in GNU tar pax 1.0 sparse files. A maliciously-crafted archive containing a large number of sparse regions can cause a Reader to read an unbounded amount of data from the archive into memory. When reading from a compressed source, a small compressed input can result in large allocations.\n",
                "markdown": "> tar.Reader does not set a maximum size on the number of sparse region data blocks in GNU tar pax 1.0 sparse files. A maliciously-crafted archive containing a large number of sparse regions can cause a Reader to read an unbounded amount of data from the archive into memory. When reading from a compressed source, a small compressed input can result in large allocations.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.16.5  |\n|Affected range  <1.24.8                   |\n|Fixed version   1.24.8                    |\n"
              },
