            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50349",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-50349"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2024-50349?s=ubuntu&n=git&ns=ubuntu&t=deb&osn=ubuntu&osv=22.04&vr=%3C1%3A2.34.1-1ubuntu1.12",
              "help": {
                "text": "Git is a fast, scalable, distributed revision control system with an unusually rich command set that provides both high-level operations and full access to internals. When Git asks for credentials via a terminal prompt (i.e. without using any credential helper), it prints out the host name for which the user is expected to provide a username and/or a password. At this stage, any URL-encoded parts have been decoded already, and are printed verbatim. This allows attackers to craft URLs that contain ANSI escape sequences that the terminal interpret to confuse users e.g. into providing passwords for trusted Git hosting sites when in fact they are then sent to untrusted sites that are under the attacker's control. This issue has been patch via commits `7725b81` and `c903985` which are included in release versions v2.48.1, v2.47.2, v2.46.3, v2.45.3, v2.44.3, v2.43.6, v2.42.4, v2.41.3, and v2.40.4. Users are advised to upgrade. Users unable to upgrade should avoid cloning from untrusted URLs, especially recursive clones.\n",
                "markdown": "> Git is a fast, scalable, distributed revision control system with an unusually rich command set that provides both high-level operations and full access to internals. When Git asks for credentials via a terminal prompt (i.e. without using any credential helper), it prints out the host name for which the user is expected to provide a username and/or a password. At this stage, any URL-encoded parts have been decoded already, and are printed verbatim. This allows attackers to craft URLs that contain ANSI escape sequences that the terminal interpret to confuse users e.g. into providing passwords for trusted Git hosting sites when in fact they are then sent to untrusted sites that are under the attacker's control. This issue has been patch via commits `7725b81` and `c903985` which are included in release versions v2.48.1, v2.47.2, v2.46.3, v2.45.3, v2.44.3, v2.43.6, v2.42.4, v2.41.3, and v2.40.4. Users are advised to upgrade. Users unable to upgrade should avoid cloning from untrusted URLs, especially recursive clones.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                                         |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:deb/ubuntu/git@1%3A2.34.1-1ubuntu1.4?os_distro=jammy&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=22.04  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <1:2.34.1-1ubuntu1.12                                                                     |\n|Fixed version                                                                  1:2.34.1-1ubuntu1.12                                                                      |\n|[[CVSS Score 4.7] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:N/I:L/A:N]]                                                                                            |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1:2.34.1-1ubuntu1.12",
                "cvssV3": 4.7,
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "cvssV3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:N/I:L/A:N",
                "fixed_version": "1:2.34.1-1ubuntu1.12",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/git@1%3A2.34.1-1ubuntu1.4?os_distro=jammy&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=22.04"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.7",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-30258",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-30258"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-30258?s=ubuntu&n=gnupg2&ns=ubuntu&t=deb&osn=ubuntu&osv=22.04&vr=%3C2.2.27-3ubuntu2.3",
              "help": {
                "text": "In GnuPG before 2.5.5, if a user chooses to import a certificate with certain crafted subkey data that lacks a valid backsig or that has incorrect usage flags, the user loses the ability to verify signatures made from certain other signing keys, aka a \"verification DoS.\"\n",
                "markdown": "> In GnuPG before 2.5.5, if a user chooses to import a certificate with certain crafted subkey data that lacks a valid backsig or that has incorrect usage flags, the user loses the ability to verify signatures made from certain other signing keys, aka a \"verification DoS.\"\n\n|                                                                                                                                                                        |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:deb/ubuntu/gnupg2@2.2.27-3ubuntu2.1?os_distro=jammy&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=22.04  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <2.2.27-3ubuntu2.3                                                                       |\n|Fixed version                                                                  2.2.27-3ubuntu2.3                                                                        |\n|[[CVSS Score 4.7] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]]                                                                                           |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<2.2.27-3ubuntu2.3",
                "cvssV3": 4.7,
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "cvssV3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
