            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-48303",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-48303"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2022-48303?s=ubuntu&n=tar&ns=ubuntu&t=deb&osn=ubuntu&osv=22.04&vr=%3C1.34%2Bdfsg-1ubuntu0.1.22.04.1",
              "help": {
                "text": "GNU Tar through 1.34 has a one-byte out-of-bounds read that results in use of uninitialized memory for a conditional jump. Exploitation to change the flow of control has not been demonstrated. The issue occurs in from_header in list.c via a V7 archive in which mtime has approximately 11 whitespace characters.\n",
                "markdown": "> GNU Tar through 1.34 has a one-byte out-of-bounds read that results in use of uninitialized memory for a conditional jump. Exploitation to change the flow of control has not been demonstrated. The issue occurs in from_header in list.c via a V7 archive in which mtime has approximately 11 whitespace characters.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                                       |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:deb/ubuntu/tar@1.34%2Bdfsg-1build3?os_distro=jammy&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=22.04  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <1.34+dfsg-1ubuntu0.1.22.04.1                                                           |\n|Fixed version                                                                  1.34+dfsg-1ubuntu0.1.22.04.1                                                            |\n|[[CVSS Score 5.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]]                                                                                          |\n"
