            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-51385",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-51385"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2023-51385?s=ubuntu&n=openssh&ns=ubuntu&t=deb&osn=ubuntu&osv=22.04&vr=%3C1%3A8.9p1-3ubuntu0.6",
              "help": {
                "text": "In ssh in OpenSSH before 9.6, OS command injection might occur if a user name or host name has shell metacharacters, and this name is referenced by an expansion token in certain situations. For example, an untrusted Git repository can have a submodule with shell metacharacters in a user name or host name.\n",
                "markdown": "> In ssh in OpenSSH before 9.6, OS command injection might occur if a user name or host name has shell metacharacters, and this name is referenced by an expansion token in certain situations. For example, an untrusted Git repository can have a submodule with shell metacharacters in a user name or host name.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                                   |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:deb/ubuntu/openssh@1%3A8.9p1-3?os_distro=jammy&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=22.04  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <1:8.9p1-3ubuntu0.6                                                                 |\n|Fixed version                                                                  1:8.9p1-3ubuntu0.6                                                                  |\n|[[CVSS Score 6.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N]]                                                                                      |\n"
