            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-20329",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-20329: Improper Validation of Specified Type of Input"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2021-20329?s=github&n=mongo-driver&ns=go.mongodb.org&t=golang&vr=%3C1.5.1",
              "help": {
                "text": "Specific cstrings input may not be properly validated in the MongoDB Go Driver when marshalling Go objects into BSON. A malicious user could use a Go object with specific string to potentially inject additional fields into marshalled documents. This issue affects all MongoDB GO Drivers up to (and including) 1.5.0.\n",
                "markdown": "> Specific cstrings input may not be properly validated in the MongoDB Go Driver when marshalling Go objects into BSON. A malicious user could use a Go object with specific string to potentially inject additional fields into marshalled documents. This issue affects all MongoDB GO Drivers up to (and including) 1.5.0.\n\n|                                                                                                                             |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:golang/go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver@1.1.2  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <1.5.1                                        |\n|Fixed version                                                                  1.5.1                                         |\n|[[CVSS Score 6.8] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N]]                                                |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.5.1",
